From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yingqian Yang <yingqian@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 08 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nan_de: add nan_de_pause_service() for single-radio
 concurrency (FR203519)

QCC730 has a single radio, so NAN USD publish/subscribe and the WiFi
STA association scan/connect flow compete for the same channel. During
WiFiPAF commissioning, once the commissioner has received the WiFi
credentials over NAN and the device needs to scan+associate to the AP,
the periodic NAN Publish SDF broadcast (and any solicited replies it
triggers) must stop hogging the radio -- otherwise the WiFi scan is
starved and commissioning stalls.

nan_de already has a per-service "pause" mechanism (pause_state_end /
sel_peer_addr / sel_peer_id fields on struct nan_de_service), but it
was previously only set internally by nan_de itself after a solicited
publish response, as a short anti-flood cooldown against one specific
peer. This adds nan_de_pause_service(), a public API that:

  - Extends the pause window to an arbitrary duration (used with 120s
    by qcc730_nan_glue_allow_wifi_scan() in qcc730_nan_de_glue.c,
    committed separately in the qcc730 project).
  - Always overrides sel_peer to a dummy NAN cluster address
    (51:6f:9a:01:00:00) that no real subscriber can present as its own
    address. This makes the existing pause_state peer-mismatch check
    suppress ALL incoming subscribe SDFs during the pause window,
    regardless of which peer previously triggered a response --
    without this override, the active commissioner's SDF flood would
    still match sel_peer and trigger solicited publish TX (and the
    RXP DISABLE0=0xffffffff config path), blocking the WiFi scan the
    pause was meant to protect.

The publish service slot itself stays alive during the pause (only
periodic/solicited broadcast is suppressed), so nan_de_transmit()
(follow-up TX, used to deliver WiFiNetworkEnable's response back to
the commissioner) continues to work normally.

Change-Id: I5f8f2c1a3d6b4e0a9c7d2b5e8f1a4c6d0b3e7f92
Signed-off-by: Yingqian Yang <yingqian@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/common/nan_de.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/common/nan_de.h |  6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/common/nan_de.c b/src/common/nan_de.c
index 12fad3112..c42debc17 100644
--- a/src/common/nan_de.c
+++ b/src/common/nan_de.c
@@ -1285,6 +1285,32 @@ void nan_de_cancel_publish(struct nan_de *de, int publish_id)
 }


+void nan_de_pause_service(struct nan_de *de, int service_id, unsigned int seconds)
+{
+	static const u8 nan_cluster_addr[ETH_ALEN] = {0x51, 0x6f, 0x9a, 0x01, 0x00, 0x00};
+	struct nan_de_service *srv;
+
+	if (!de || service_id < 1 || service_id > NAN_DE_MAX_SERVICE)
+		return;
+	srv = de->service[service_id - 1];
+	if (!srv)
+		return;
+	os_get_reltime(&srv->pause_state_end);
+	srv->pause_state_end.sec += seconds;
+	/* Always override sel_peer to the NAN cluster addr (a dummy value that
+	 * no real subscriber will present as its own address).  This ensures
+	 * ALL incoming subscribe SDFs are treated as "from a different peer"
+	 * by the pause_state check, suppressing every solicited publish
+	 * response regardless of whether a peer was already discovered.
+	 * Without this override, if sel_peer was already set to the active
+	 * commissioner, its SDF flood would still trigger solicited publish
+	 * TX responses (and DISABLE0=0xffffffff), blocking WiFi scan. */
+	os_memcpy(srv->sel_peer_addr, nan_cluster_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+	srv->sel_peer_id = 1;
+	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "NAN: pause_service id=%d for %u s", service_id, seconds);
+}
+
+
 int nan_de_update_publish(struct nan_de *de, int publish_id,
 			  const struct wpabuf *ssi)
 {
diff --git a/src/common/nan_de.h b/src/common/nan_de.h
index 62235064b..11c7b3d0f 100644
--- a/src/common/nan_de.h
+++ b/src/common/nan_de.h
@@ -109,6 +109,12 @@ int nan_de_publish(struct nan_de *de, const char *service_name,

 void nan_de_cancel_publish(struct nan_de *de, int publish_id);

+/* Pause periodic SDF broadcasts for a publish service for |seconds| seconds.
+ * The service slot stays alive so nan_de_transmit() (follow-up TX) still works.
+ * Used by qcc730_nan_glue_allow_wifi_scan() before initiating WiFi association
+ * scan to stop NAN TX from blocking the radio on the discovery channel. */
+void nan_de_pause_service(struct nan_de *de, int service_id, unsigned int seconds);
+
 int nan_de_update_publish(struct nan_de *de, int publish_id,
 			  const struct wpabuf *ssi);

--
2.34.1
